diff --git a/doc/p2mr-rescue.md b/doc/p2mr-rescue.md
index 1ee95ea..c5b75a6 100644
--- a/doc/p2mr-rescue.md
+++ b/doc/p2mr-rescue.md
@@ -240,3 +240,16 @@ There is no RPC to make proofs or rescue transactions: proofs are made off the n
   vectors.
 - `bench_bitcoin -filter='.*P2MRRescue.*'`: the verifier, valid and in its most expensive invalid
   form, and the whole path of a check.
+
+## Kill switch
+
+This build carries the kill switch of the M4-R design (section 11), which is not part of the M4-R1
+release: from the height of the buried deployment `p2mr_rescue_end` (`ARK0_RESCUE_END_HEIGHT` on
+Ark-0, not set; `-signetrescueend=<height>` on another custom signet, above `-signetrescue`;
+`-testactivationheight=p2mr_rescue_end@<height>` on regtest), blocks are checked with
+`SCRIPT_VERIFY_P2MR_NO_RESCUE` again. It only restricts the rules, a soft fork, and needs no key. The
+mempool follows it: it checks with the restriction once the next block is at the height; the block
+before the height removes the transactions with a rescue record, with their descendants, and so does
+a reorganization that leaves the next block at or above it; `gettripwireinfo` reports `end_height`
+and stops reporting `mempool_accepts`. Rescue spends confirmed below the height stay valid.
+`feature_p2mr_rescue_killswitch.py` tests it.
